        "original_id": "1b2c8a2b-d798-5450-9828-bf973b4da1e6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Michigan gubernatorial election, 2006; Michigan Secretary of State election, 2014\n- People: Jennifer Granholm; Dick DeVos; Ruth Johnson\n- Roles: Governor of Michigan; Lieutenant governor candidate; Michigan Secretary of State; Michigan House of Representatives member\n\nFacts:\n- On November 7, 2006, the Michigan gubernatorial election was one of 36 U.S. gubernatorial elections held that day.\n- In 2006, incumbent Democratic Governor Jennifer Granholm was re-elected in Michigan over Republican businessman Dick DeVos and three minor party candidates.\n- In 2006, Ruth Johnson was the Republican candidate for lieutenant governor as Dick DeVos's running mate.\n- Ruth Johnson was a former member of the Michigan House of Representatives.\n- Dick DeVos, born October 21, 1955, is an American entrepreneur-businessman and author from Michigan.\n- In 2014, incumbent Republican Michigan Secretary of State Ruth Johnson was re-elected to a second term with 53.53% of the vote.",
